2. Multiresolution Analysis: The wavelet coefficients are decomposed into different resolutions using multiresolution analysis. The computation cost of multiresolution analysis is O(N).
3. Inverse Wavelet Transform: The wavelet coefficients are transformed back into the time domain using the inverse wavelet transform. The computation cost of the inverse wavelet transform is O(N log N).

Phase Vocoder Approach:
1. Short-Time Fourier Transform (STFT): The STFT is applied to the signal to decompose it into the frequency domain. The computation cost of the STFT is O(N log N).
2. Phase Vocoder: The phase vocoder is then applied to the frequency components to resynthesize the signal. The computation cost of the phase vocoder is O(N).

In terms of computational cost, the wavelet analysis and resynthesis approach is generally more computationally expensive than the phase vocoder approach. However, the wavelet approach provides more detailed frequency information and is more robust to noise, while the phase vocoder approach is more efficient in terms of computation and can be used for real-time processing."},
