{"role": "user", "content": "Write library on c to work with JDY-41 wireless module on raspberry pi pico"},
{"role": "assistant", "content": "Here is a C library to work with the JDY-41 wireless module on the Raspberry Pi Pico:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include "pico/stdlib.h"
#include "pico/uart.h"

// UART settings for JDY-41 module 
#define UART_ID uart0
#define BAUD_RATE 9600
#define DATA_BITS 8
#define STOP_BITS 1
#define PARITY UART_PARITY_NONE

// UART buffers
char tx_buffer[256];
char rx_buffer[256];

// UART instance 
uart_inst_t *uart;

// Initialize UART for JDY-41 module
void jdy41_init() {
  uart = uart_init(UART_ID, BAUD_RATE);
  gpio_set_function(UART_TX_PIN, GPIO_FUNC_UART);
  gpio_set_function(UART_RX_PIN, GPIO_FUNC_UART);
}

// Send AT command to JDY-41 module
void jdy41_send_at(char *command) {
  sprintf(tx_buffer, "%s\r\n", command);
  uart_write_blocking(uart, tx_buffer, strlen(tx_buffer));
}

// Receive data from JDY-41 module 
void jdy41_receive() {
  uart_read_blocking(uart, rx_buffer, sizeof(rx_buffer));
  printf("%s\n", rx_buffer);
}

// Main function
int main() {
  stdio_init_all();

  // Initialize UART
  jdy41_init();

  // Send AT command
  jdy41_send_at("AT");

  // Receive response
  jdy41_receive();
}
```

This library initializes the UART, provides functions to send AT commands to the JDY-41 module and receive responses. Let me know if you have any questions!"},
